=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the repository-backed cache-then-network data port), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's
  idealized "TeslaSync/Features/Sharing/SharingTripsPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs" is mapped onto these real conventions;
  the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("SharingTrips", already mapped by
  RouteTable as Page("SharingTrips","sharing/trips",Sharing)).
- Data source: useTrips({ vehicle_id, limit: 20 }). SharingTripsSource resolves the in-scope vehicle from the shared
  IWidgetVehicleSource (native useSelectedVehicle), then reads the generated operation get_api_v1_trips through the
  shared CacheThenNetworkEngine. Faithful to the web hook, the query is NOT disabled when no vehicle is selected —
  it omits vehicle_id and reads fleet-wide; the limit is always sent. The view never performs HTTP (P1/S8 seam).
- SI display boundary (P1/S5): total_distance_m is converted to the user's distance unit via
  UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi + UnitLabels (web convertDistanceFromSI + unitPrefs.distance), fmtInt-style integer;
  total_energy_wh is read as SI watt-hours (web fmtNumber(total_energy_wh) + " Wh"); the duration mirrors the page's
  own formatDuration(start,end) rules; the date uses DateTimeVariant.Date ("MMM d, yyyy" == web formatDate). Live
  units come from AppSettingsHost.Current.ToUnitPref() and re-project on AppSettingsService.Changed.
- The page reproduces all three web regions: GlassPanel1 (recent-trips list with the 3 data states + the single
  trip-selection model — a Fluent single-select ListView = web role="listbox"/role="option"), GlassPanel2 (the
  static share-card hint), and the opt-in trip-postcard drafter (AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration, its own
  parity unit) wired to the selected trip and gated default-OFF (StaticAiFeatureGate.Off + an off-mode transport),
  so it collapses to nothing exactly like the web withAiFeature gate. The 2 GlassPanels + 3 states + 8 strings are
  this page unit's 13 parity items; the AI drafter is reproduced structurally but tracked under its own unit.
- All 8 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/en/Resources.resw (translation.sharing.trips.*); the surface
  resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names + verbatim English defaults (no new catalog
  rows required). row.drives is the native "{0} drives" template (String.Format with the drive count).
- Pre-existing blocker repaired (tightly coupled, build-breaking): the worktree's integration branch carried a bad
  merge (commit e8f7a3d744) that inserted the NotificationsArchived registration INSIDE the Locations registration
  lambda in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs, leaving the Locations lambda unclosed (one missing `return page; });`). That
  unbalanced C# (final brace depth +1) poisoned the XAML markup compiler's Roslyn type universe, so the whole app
  failed to build with WMC9999 + a cascade of bogus "Unknown type 'TsButton'/..." WMC0001 errors (84 errors). Since
  ShellWindow registration is exactly the NavigationView-registration file this prompt must edit (allowed-files
  scope), restored the Locations block's `return page; });`. App then built 0 errors / 0 warnings.

